{
  "schema_version": "psop.static-homepage-assets/1",
  "created": "2026-10-15",
  "geometry_source": "Official Microduck walk-reference XML/STL assembly: 38 source meshes, 70 assembly instances, SRC-000048 / qpos0; source geometry preserved",
  "geometry_license": "Creative Commons BY-SA-NC; upstream statement does not name a version",
  "case_boundaries": [
    "Product screenshots and the edited assembly recording come from the actual current workbench and the recorded .10 snapshot.",
    "Build runs through the CLI; the webpage displays registered knowledge snapshots. Compile execution services are not connected.",
    "The assembly movie combines two isolated scenes from the same snapshot. The head-shell close-up hides the other 68 instances through native visibility controls. Waiting, camera adjustment and intermediate automatic-assembly footage are cut. Automatic playback is native 4x; scene and motions are real recordings.",
    "Source geometry, colors and original assembly matrices are preserved. Exploded display offsets do not certify an assembly path.",
    "Rigid intersections, assembly operation eligibility and mechanical verification are distinct records; reference overlap alone does not invalidate assembly.",
    "EG and Microduck AR are teaching examples. installation-process.webp is an existing generated illustration, not a field photograph.",
    "240 paired experiments and ar-demo-25s.mp4 concern the earlier mechanical-arm work, not current Microduck measurements.",
    "psop-overview.pdf is a historical research presentation, not the current product specification."
  ],
  "serving": "Standalone local assets only; no runtime API, CDN or external font. Video and PDF are requested only on explicit interaction. Non-hero images and 3D dependencies load on demand.",
